  - TypeFullName: Basis.Scripts.BasisSdk.Players.BasisLocalHeightInformation
    MemberName: BasisLocalHeightInformation
    Kind: Type
    ParamCount: 0
    ParamNames: []
    ParamDocs: []
    Summary: "Serializable container for player/avatar height metrics and scale ratios.\n
      Tracks measured eye heights and arm spans for both the user (player) and the
      avatar,\n along with precomputed scale ratios and the currently selected height/scale
      pair."
    Remarks: "Use PickRatio(BasisSelectedHeightMode) to populate the\n SelectedPlayerHeight,
      SelectedAvatarHeight,\n SelectedPlayerToDefaultScale, and SelectedAvatarToAvatarDefaultScale
      fields\n based on the chosen mode (ArmSpan, EyeHeight, or Custom).\n \n\n\n
      Note on the `Custom` branch: the scale computation uses\n BasisLocalPlayer.DefaultAvatarEyeHeight
      for the player scale and\n BasisLocalPlayer.DefaultPlayerEyeHeight for the
      avatar scale. Verify this is intentional."
    Returns: 
    Value: 
    Examples: []
    TypeParamNames: []
    TypeParamDocs: []
